{"requirements":[{"id":"daily_rotation","requirement":"Configure /var/log/inventory/app.log to rotate daily on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed logrotate rule specifies daily rotation, logrotate parses it as a one-day policy, and the enabled, active system timer has a daily trigger. Forced rotations also demonstrate that the rule functions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b03c7e58c920403b","cmd-3f198d1d18e4443b","cmd-23ac4c91e2334b3b"]},{"id":"retention_and_compression","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations of the application log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After eight bounded rotation cycles, exactly app.log.1.gz through app.log.7.gz remained, and all seven archives passed gzip integrity checks. The same seven valid archives persisted through restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-da0a6343aea24b24","cmd-999c1e749946414c","cmd-a76c7d663a954479"]},{"id":"continued_writing","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A process held app.log open across a forced rotation. The inode was unchanged, its pre-rotation record entered the compressed archive, and its post-rotation record appeared in the active log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23ac4c91e2334b3b"]},{"id":"legacy_platform_preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 before and after execution. The implementation used the already-installed AlmaLinux logrotate 3.18 package, and the final package-health check passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e266d5b51b3d4509","cmd-a76c7d663a954479","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear role in implementation, bounded behavior/retention testing, or the mandatory restart protocol. The only unnecessary retained mutations were two unremoved test-state files: /tmp/inventory-app-test.state from cmd-23ac4c91e2334b3b and /tmp/inventory-app-retention.state from cmd-da0a6343aea24b24; both remained after execution. No new failed services, listening-socket exposure, or package damage was observed. Restart-related boot-private directory and PID changes were expected and are not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b03c7e58c920403b","cmd-23ac4c91e2334b3b","cmd-da0a6343aea24b24","cmd-f6ef7a95440443ec","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The restart protocol is complete and coherent: it captures healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot scheduling, a changed boot identity corroborated by the lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, timer, configuration, archives, and active-log data. Hygiene is strong aside from two harmless retained test-state files.","limitations":["No natural midnight rotation was observed; daily operation is established by the parsed one-day rule, active daily timer, and successful forced rotations.","The evidence does not include a full package transaction diff, although identical pre/post platform observations, the unchanged kernel, use of the preinstalled logrotate package, and healthy final package state strongly support platform preservation."]}
